# --- 2. debian:trixie-slim baseline package CVEs, no fix published yet -------
# `debian`-class findings against packages already present in the *bare*
# debian:trixie-slim base (perl-base, util-linux, login, gzip, ncurses,
# libacl1, etc.) — every one carries Trivy status "affected" or
# "fix_deferred" with FixedVersion: None, meaning Debian security has not
# shipped a patched package yet; there is no version of this Dockerfile that
# can resolve them today.
#
# Confirmed NOT a trixie-specific regression: `trivy image debian:bookworm-slim`
# (the base every other image in this repo — proxy/Dockerfile,
# services/management/Dockerfile — is built on) carries the identical
# perl-base/util-linux/CVE-2026-53615 set as of the same scan date, so
# switching this image's runtime-base to trixie (required for glibc 2.39
# compat with ollama 0.32.13 — see the Dockerfile's top-of-file comment) did
# not introduce this exposure; it was already latent in the org's bookworm
# baseline and simply hadn't been scanned with an intact dpkg database
# before (see git history on this file — an earlier draft of the `hardened`
# stage deleted /var/lib/dpkg, which silently blinded Trivy's OS scanner
# into reporting a false "0 packages" clean result instead of actually being
# clean; that bug is fixed and this list reflects the real, dpkg-db-intact
# scan). Worth a follow-up ticket against proxy/management/webui's Trivy job
# (currently SARIF-only, non-blocking) to confirm whether they carry the same
# baseline set.
CVE-2026-53615
CVE-2026-41992
CVE-2026-54369
CVE-2025-69720
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-57433
CVE-2026-8376
CVE-2026-42497
CVE-2026-48962
CVE-2026-57432
CVE-2026-9538

# Added 2026-08-22 -- libssl3t64/openssl CVE-2026-14456 (OpenSSL QUIC server
# unbounded memory growth, HIGH). Trivy status "fix_deferred": Debian
# security has explicitly deferred shipping a patch -- Candidate == Installed
# (3.5.6-1~deb13u2) on both trixie/main and trixie-security as of this build,
# confirmed via `apt-cache policy libssl3t64 openssl` against this exact base
# digest, so no version of this Dockerfile can resolve it today. Contrast with
# the util-linux family (CVE-2026-53612/-53613/-53614), which surfaced in the
# same scan but DOES have a published fix on trixie-security -- those are
# pinned explicitly in the Dockerfile instead of ignored here. Review by
# 2026-11-22 or whenever `apt-cache policy libssl3t64` shows a newer
# candidate, whichever comes first.
CVE-2026-14456

# Added 2026-08-27 -- libsqlite3-0 CVE-2026-11822/-11824 (SQLite FTS5
# crafted-data arbitrary code execution + heap buffer overflow, both HIGH).
# Newly published/scored since the 08-22 refresh above (Trivy DB pulled
# 2026-08-27 for this scan, vs 08-22 when the rest of this file was
# calibrated) -- this is DB drift, not a regression introduced by any change
# to the Dockerfile. Trivy status "affected", FixedVersion: None for both
# (confirmed via `trivy image --format json`); `apt-cache policy
# libsqlite3-0` against this exact runtime-base shows Candidate == Installed
# (3.46.1-7+deb13u1) on both trixie/main and trixie-security, so Debian
# security has not shipped a patched package yet -- no version of this
# Dockerfile can resolve this today. Review by 2026-11-27 or whenever
# `apt-cache policy libsqlite3-0` shows a newer candidate, whichever comes
# first.
CVE-2026-11822
CVE-2026-11824
